      "writtenOn": "2017-07-07T04:32:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why In_system instead of Vndk? It implies more than just whether it\u0027s in the system partition or not (ABI, whether it\u0027s eligible for extension, etc)\n\nIt\u0027s not obvious that is_system would depend on vendor_available without looking at the documentation -- I would assume that it would default to true if !vendor, which isn\u0027t what you\u0027re going for here.\n\nOnce we add the single-process differentiator, a grouping starts to make sense, but I can\u0027t think of a good name for it:\n\n  \u003cvndk\u003e: {\n      \u003cis\u003e: true,\n      single_process: true,\n  }",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 172,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 172,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "1d40739be1768e3504ec5749368044262e87f76c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5ff31d45_12b17b7b",
        "filename": "cc/cc.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 172,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-07T09:02:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "vndk: {\n    enabled: true // implies vendor_available:true, default is false\n    support_system_process: true // true means this is VNDK-SP, default is false\n}\n\n?",
      "parentUuid": "12d0e6a8_20ecf5ce",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 172,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 172,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "1d40739be1768e3504ec5749368044262e87f76c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f2a253a7_2e6cd0b8",
        "filename": "cc/cc.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 172,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146974
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-07T09:48:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Still it depends on `vendor_available: true`.\nSo we may have following four kinds of modules.\n1. vendor_available: false,\n2. vendor_available: true, vndk: false,\n3. vendor_available: true, vndk: true, vndksp: false,\n4. vendor_available: true, vndk: true, vndksp: true.\n\nIf we put these in a group, should they be like below?\n\n1. vendor_available: false,\n2. vendor_available: true,\n3. vendor_available: true,\n   vndk: {\n       enabled: true,\n   }\n4. vendor_available: true,\n   vndk: {\n       enabled: true,\n       support_system_process: true,\n   }",
      "parentUuid": "5ff31d45_12b17b7b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 172,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 172,
        "endChar": 10
      },
